# V19 multi-extractor benchmark (extractors.py) -- API key for the Gemini
# engine (gemini-3.8-flash). Copy this file to .env and fill in real values;
# .env itself is gitignored and must NEVER be committed.
GEMINI_API_KEY=

# Hosted Qwen3-VL test ("qwen3_vl" engine, extractors.run_qwen3_vl_hosted) --
# calls the model on Hugging Face's hosted inference infrastructure directly.
# NO local model weights are downloaded/run for this path.
HF_TOKEN=
# V19f: aligned to the same 4B model validated for the local engine below,
# per explicit user policy that local and hosted Qwen3-VL stay in sync.
QWEN_MODEL=Qwen/Qwen3-VL-4B-Instruct
# Optional: force a specific HF Inference Provider (e.g. "featherless-ai").
# Leave unset -- vlm.py auto-detects the model's live provider if HF's
# default "auto" routing can't find one (confirmed necessary for
# Qwen/Qwen3-VL-2B-Instruct, which was served by featherless-ai only -- may
# differ for the 4B model above, not yet re-verified).
HF_PROVIDER=

# Local Qwen3-VL test ("qwen3_vl_local" engine, extractors.run_qwen3_vl_local)
# -- runs entirely on-device (vlm.py's _load()), no network/HF_TOKEN needed.
# Model weights auto-discovered under models/Qwen3-VL-4B-Instruct/ (see
# vlm.DEFAULT_LOCAL_CANDIDATES, falls back to models/Qwen2-VL-2B-Instruct/ if
# the 4B weights aren't present) once downloaded there; set VLM_MODEL_PATH
# only if you keep them somewhere else.
# VLM_MODEL_PATH=
# Re-verified on an RTX 4060 Laptop (8.6GB VRAM) with the 4-bit-quantized 4B
# model at the 1600 default: ~22-26s/document, no OOM (see vlm.py's comment
# above extract_direct_semantic_local). The earlier note below about a
# 2GB-VRAM MX230/2B-model combo needing VLM_MAX_SIDE_FULL=640 (and still
# reading handwriting at ~0% accuracy even then) was measured on
# fundamentally different, much more constrained hardware -- do not assume
# it applies here; only lower this if you hit CUDA OOM on your own hardware.
# VLM_MAX_SIDE_FULL=640
# VLM_LOAD_IN_4BIT=auto  # "auto" = on whenever CUDA is selected; "0" forces full precision
# On by default (see vlm.HOSTED_SIGNATURE_VOTE_COUNT / VLM_SIGNATURE_VOTE_COUNT):
# both engines now run the signature fields 3x and take a lenient any-present
# vote to counter VLM non-determinism. Set to 1 to go back to a single local
# call if 3x inference is too slow on your hardware.
# VLM_SIGNATURE_VOTE_COUNT=3

# V20 -- HYBRID engine ("qwen3_vl_local_yolos", extractors.
# run_qwen3_vl_local_yolos) -- additive to qwen3_vl_local above, does NOT
# change it. Same Qwen3-VL Local semantic extraction, but signature fields
# come from a local YOLOS signature detector (signature_detector.py)
# instead of Qwen's own judgment. HARD LOCAL-ONLY: this engine never
# downloads weights at runtime and never calls any hosted/network API for
# either component -- if either Qwen3-VL local OR the signature-detector
# weights below are missing, the engine refuses to process ANY document
# (extractors._hybrid_readiness / run_qwen3_vl_local_yolos's pre-flight
# gate) rather than running partially.
#
# Weights: mdefrance/yolos-tiny-signature-detection on Hugging Face Hub --
# Apache-2.0, NOT gated, freely downloadable (unlike Tech4Humans' YOLOv8
# signature detector, originally targeted but abandoned because that repo
# is gated -- requires manually accepting access on the HF website first,
# with no scriptable path around it). Auto-discovered under
# models/yolos-tiny-signature-detection/ once placed there (via
# transformers' AutoImageProcessor/AutoModelForObjectDetection
# .save_pretrained -- see handover.md); set SIGNATURE_DETECTOR_MODEL_PATH
# only if you keep it somewhere else.
# SIGNATURE_DETECTOR_MODEL_PATH=
# YOLOS detection-proposal confidence threshold (NOT the same as the
# present/uncertain boundary below 0.6 in extractors.py, which is applied
# AFTER a detection is found) -- 0.25 is a conventional low default, only
# spot-checked against ONE real document this session (see handover.md);
# re-tune once more real signed documents have been run through it.
# SIGNATURE_DETECTOR_CONF_THRESHOLD=0.25
